other-options" class="sidebar-link">Other options</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="../../how-to/take-snapshot/" class="sidebar-link">Take a snapshot</a></li><li><a href="../../how-to/store-play-videos/" class="sidebar-link">Store &#x26; play videos</a></li><li><a href="../../how-to/host-git-repo/" class="sidebar-link">Host a Git-style repo</a></li><li><a href="../../how-to/move-ipfs-installation/move-ipfs-installation/" class="sidebar-link">Move an IPFS installation</a></li><li><a href="../../how-to/content-addressing-data-sets/" class="sidebar-link">Content addressing data sets</a></li></ul></section></li><li><section class="sidebar-group collapsable depth-0"><p class="sidebar-heading"><span>Websites on IPFS</span> <span class="arrow right"></span></p> <!----></section></li><li><section class="sidebar-group collapsable depth-0"><p class="sidebar-heading"><span>IPFS on the web</span> <span class="arrow right"></span></p> <!----></section></li><li><section class="sidebar-group collapsable depth-0"><p class="sidebar-heading"><span>IPNS</span> <span class="arrow right"></span></p> <!----></section></li><li><section class="sidebar-group collapsable depth-0"><p class="sidebar-heading"><span>IPFS Gateway</span> <span class="arrow right"></span></p> <!----></section></li><li><section class="sidebar-group collapsable depth-0"><p class="sidebar-heading"><span>IPFS Companion</span> <span class="arrow right"></span></p> <!----></section></li><li><section class="sidebar-group collapsable depth-0"><p class="sidebar-heading"><span>IPFS &#x26; Blockchain Networks</span> <span class="arrow right"></span></p> <!----></section></li><li><section class="sidebar-group collapsable depth-0"><p class="sidebar-heading"><span>Privacy and Encryption</span> <span class="arrow right"></span></p> <!----></section></li></ul> </aside> <main class="page" data-v-5b0b93f5=""> <div class="theme-default-content content__default" data-v-5b0b93f5=""><h1 id="work-with-remote-pinning-services"><a href="#work-with-remote-pinning-services" class="header-anchor">#</a> Work with remote pinning services</h1> <p><strong>Pinning</strong> in IPFS is a process that ensures that the pinned data is exempt from routine <a href="../../concepts/persistence/#garbage-collection">garbage collection</a> and is therefore always available. In addition to <a href="../../how-to/pin-files/">locally pinning files</a>, you can use a <strong>remote pinning service</strong>, which abstracts this responsibility away from a local, individual node.
The appropriate solution depends on your particular use case.</p> <ol><li>Determine whether to <a href="#when-to-use-a-remote-pinning-service">use an existing service</a> or <a href="#when-to-create-your-own-service">create your own</a>.</li> <li>Follow the appropriate steps:
<ul><li><a href="#use-a-third-party-pinning-service">Use an existing service</a></li> <li><a href="#create-your-own-pinning-service">Create your own service</a></li></ul></li></ol> <h2 id="when-to-use-a-remote-pinning-service"><a href="#when-to-use-a-remote-pinning-service" class="header-anchor">#</a> When to use a remote pinning service</h2> <p>If you have one local IPFS node that's always running, local pinning ensures that important data is persisted and never garbage collected. On the other hand, if your architecture is more complex, an existing or custom remote pinning service may be useful, especially if:</p> <ul><li>Your local node isn't always online, but data must be consistently available.</li> <li>You require a persistent backup of your local node's files.</li> <li>Your local node does not have enough disk space.</li> <li>You run more than one IPFS node, and would like to use one or more of those nodes as your preferred location for permanent storage.</li></ul> <p>If you've decided that an existing service is right for you, learn <a href="#use-a-third-party-pinning-service">how to use an existing service</a></p> <h2 id="when-to-create-your-own-service"><a href="#when-to-create-your-own-service" class="header-anchor">#</a> When to create your own service</h2> <p>If existing third-party pinning services don't meet your needs, you can create your own. Any remote pinning service compatible with the <a href="https://ipfs.github.io/pinning-services-api-spec" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IPFS Pinning Service API<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a> can be added as a custom pinning service. This might be useful in circumstances like:</p> <ul><li>Designating your own IPFS node(s) as the preferred location for permanent storage.</li> <li>Running a private pinning service for friends, as a business, as a public service, etc.</li></ul> <div class="custom-block warning"><p class="custom-block-title">WARNING</p> <p>Your service must use the <a href="https://ipfs.github.io/pinning-services-api-spec" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IPFS Pinning Service API<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a> in order to be interoperable with clients using <a href="../../reference/kubo/cli/#ipfs-pin-remote"><code>ipfs pin remote</code></a> commands.</p></div> <p>If you've decided that creating your own pinning service is right for you, learn <a href="#create-your-own-pinning-service">how to create your own pinning service</a>.</p> <h2 id="use-a-third-party-pinning-service"><a href="#use-a-third-party-pinning-service" class="header-anchor">#</a> Use a third-party pinning service</h2> <p>Third-party pinning services allow you to purchase pinning capacity for important data. Each service has its own approach to pinning data and managing pins, so users should do their research to ensure that the service meets their particular needs. Service providers include, but are not limited to:</p> <ul><li><a href="https://pinata.cloud/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pinata<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a></li> <li><a href="https://filebase.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Filebase<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a></li></ul> <div class="custom-block callout"><p>As of June 2023, <a href="https://filebase.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Filebase<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a> and <a href="https://pinata.cloud/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pinata<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a> support the <a href="https://github.com/ipfs/pinning-services-api-spec" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IPFS Pinning Service API endpoint<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a>.</p></div> <p>To add and use a remote pinning service directly in IPFS, you'll first need to have an account with that service.</p> <p>The method by which you add a remote pinning service depends on the way in which you are using IPFS:</p> <ul><li><a href="#ipfs-desktop-or-ipfs-web-ui">IPFS Desktop or IPFS Web UI</a></li> <li><a href="#ipfs-kubo">IPFS Kubo</a></li></ul> <h3 id="ipfs-desktop-or-ipfs-web-ui"><a href="#ipfs-desktop-or-ipfs-web-ui" class="header-anchor">#</a> IPFS Desktop or IPFS Web UI</h3> <p>You can add your favorite pinning service(s) to <a href="../../install/ipfs-desktop/">IPFS Desktop</a> or <a href="https://github.com/ipfs/ipfs-webui" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web UI<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a> directly, enabling you to pin and unpin items via a UI similar to how you would add or remove local pins.</p> <p>First, <a href="#add-a-pinning-service-in-the-ui">add the pinning service</a>. Then, you can <a href="#use-a-pinning-service-in-the-ui">use it</a>.</p> <h4 id="add-a-pinning-service-in-the-ui"><a href="#add-a-pinning-service-in-the-ui" class="header-anchor">#</a> Add a pinning service in the UI</h4> <p>To add a new pinning service to IPFS Desktop or Web UI:</p> <ol><li><p>Start IPFS Desktop or Web UI</p></li> <li><p>In <strong>Settings</strong> , navigate to <strong>Pinning Services</strong>.</p></li> <li><p>Click the <strong>Add Service</strong> button.</p> <p><img src="../../assets/img/add-service.2ea75169.jpg" alt="The Desktop/Web UI Settings screen, ready for adding a new pinning service" loading="lazy"></p></li> <li><p>In the pop up, select your chosen pinning service.</p> <p>If the pinning service you'd like to use isn't listed in that modal, click <strong>Add a custom one</strong> to add any remote pinning service that supports the <a href="https://github.com/ipfs/pinning-services-api-spec#adoption" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IPFS Pinning Service API spec<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a>.</p> <p><img src="../../assets/img/add-service-picker.338b425d.jpg" alt="Desktop/Web UI modal for selecting a pinning service to add" loading="lazy"></p></li> <li><p>Next, enter the following information:</p> <ul><li>A <strong>nickname</strong> for this service. This can be helpful if, for example, you want to add two accounts from the same service.</li> <li>Your service's <strong>API endpoint URL</strong>. This field only appears if you've selected a custom pinning service.</li> <li>You <strong>secret access token</strong>, provided to you by the pinning service. See your specific pinning service documentation for more info.</li></ul> <p>Example using Pinata and <a href="https://app.pinata.cloud/keys" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">pinata.cloud/keys<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a>:
<img src="../../assets/img/add-service-pinata-token.b8063b98.jpg" alt="Pinata secret access token" loading="lazy"></p> <p>Example using Filebase and <a href="https://console.filebase.com/keys" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">console.filebase.com/keys<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a>:
<img src="../../assets/img/add-service-filebase-token.e94454f9.png" alt="Filebase secret access token" loading="lazy"></p> <p>Comparison between an existing third-party service and a custom service:</p> <table><thead><tr><th>Third-party service (e.g., Pinata)</th> <th>Custom service</th></tr></thead> <tbody><tr><td><img src="../../assets/img/add-service-pinata.7ca72c09.jpg" alt="Adding Pinata in Desktop/Web UI" loading="lazy"></td> <td><img src="../../assets/img/add-service-custom.e6c86cb6.jpg" alt="Adding custom pinning service in Desktop/Web UI" loading="lazy"></td></tr></tbody></table></li> <li><p>Click <strong>Save</strong>. Your new pinning service is added to the <strong>Pinning Services</strong> section of your <strong>Settings</strong> screen.</p> <p><img src="../../assets/img/added-service.389c8f13.jpg" alt="Desktop/Web UI Settings screen with a new pinning service added" loading="lazy"></p></li></ol> <h4 id="use-a-pinning-service-in-the-ui"><a href="#use-a-pinning-service-in-the-ui" class="header-anchor">#</a> Use a pinning service in the UI</h4> <p>Once you've <a href="#add-a-pinning-service-in-the-ui">added a pinning service</a>, you can quickly pin or unpin files to your new pinning service directly from the UI.</p> <p>To pin a file in the UI:</p> <ol><li><p>Navigate to the <strong>Files</strong> screen.</p></li> <li><p>Right-click any file or click the <strong>three dots</strong> action icon in the files list</p></li> <li><p>Select <strong>Set pinning</strong>:</p> <p><img src="../../assets/img/set-pinning.9e80035b.jpg" alt="Desktop/Web UI Files screen with the action menu open and &#x22;Set pinning&#x22; visible" loading="lazy"></p></li></ol> <h3 id="ipfs-kubo"><a href="#ipfs-kubo" class="header-anchor">#</a> IPFS Kubo</h3> <p>IPFS Kubo provides the <a href="../../reference/kubo/cli/#ipfs-pin-remote"><code>ipfs pin remote</code></a> command to simplify remote pinning operations. The built-in pinning service API client executes all the necessary remote calls.</p> <p>To use a remote pinning service with Kubo</p> <h4 id="adding-a-new-pinning-service-to-kubo"><a href="#adding-a-new-pinning-service-to-kubo" class="header-anchor">#</a> Adding a new pinning service to Kubo</h4> <p>To add a new pinning service:</p> <ol><li><p>Open a terminal.</p></li> <li><p>Use the <a href="https://docs.ipfs.tech/reference/kubo/cli/#ipfs-pin-remote-service-add" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>pin remote service add</code><span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a> command to add the service:</p> <ul><li>Give the service a <code>&#x3C;nickname></code> For example, this can be helpful if you want to add two accounts from the same service.</li> <li>Add an <code>&#x3C;endpoint></code>, which is supplied to you by the pinning service. Example: <code>https://my-pin-service.example.com/api-endpoint</code></li> <li>Add an <code>&#x3C;accessToken></code>. This is the unique secret token provided to you by the pinning service. Check the service's documentation for more info.</li></ul> <div class="language-shell extra-class"><pre class="language-shell"><code>ipfs pin remote <span class="token function">service</span> <span class="token function">add</span> <span class="token operator">&#x3C;</span>nickname<span class="token operator">></span> <span class="token operator">&#x3C;</span>endpoint<span class="token operator">></span> <span class="token operator">&#x3C;</span>accessToken<span class="token operator">></span>
</code></pre></div></li></ol> <p>Success. You can now <a href="#use-a-pinning-service-in-kubo">use the pinning service</a>.</p> <h4 id="use-a-pinning-service-in-kubo"><a href="#use-a-pinning-service-in-kubo" class="header-anchor">#</a> Use a pinning service in Kubo</h4> <p>The following section describes various commands that allow you to use an added pinning service in Kubo. In each example, replace <code>&#x3C;nickname></code> with the unique name you gave the pinning service when you added it.</p> <p>To pin a CID under a human-readable name:</p> <div class="language-shell extra-class"><pre class="language-shell"><code>$ ipfs pin remote <span class="token function">add</span> <span class="token parameter variable">--service</span><span class="token operator">=</span><span class="token operator">&#x3C;</span>nickname<span class="token operator">></span> <span class="token parameter variable">--name</span><span class="token operator">=</span>war-and-peace.txt bafybeib32tuqzs2wrc52rdt56cz73sqe3qu2deqdudssspnu4gbezmhig4
</code></pre></div><p>To list successful pins:</p> <div class="language-shell extra-class"><pre class="language-shell"><code>$ ipfs pin remote <span class="token function">ls</span> <span class="token parameter variable">--service</span><span class="token operator">=</span>nickname
</code></pre></div><p>To list pending pins:</p> <div class="language-shell extra-class"><pre class="language-shell"><code>$ ipfs pin remote <span class="token function">ls</span> <span class="token parameter variable">--service</span><span class="token operator">=</span>nickname <span class="token parameter variable">--status</span><span class="token operator">=</span>queued,pinning,failed
</code></pre></div><p>For more commands and general help:</p> <div class="language-shell extra-class"><pre class="language-shell"><code>$ ipfs pin remote <span class="token parameter variable">--help</span>
</code></pre></div><h2 id="create-your-own-pinning-service"><a href="#create-your-own-pinning-service" class="header-anchor">#</a> Create your own pinning service</h2> <p>If you're interested in creating your own pinning service for personal or shared use, you have two options:</p> <ol><li><p><a href="https://github.com/ipfs/pinning-services-api-spec#code-generation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Generate a client and server from the OpenAPI spec<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a></p></li> <li><p><a href="https://github.com/ipfs/pinning-services-api-spec#adoption" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Reuse an existing solution<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a> to reduce development time.</p></li></ol> <p>Note: the <a href="https://github.com/ipfs/pinning-services-api-spec" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pinning Service API spec<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a> is frozen and its repository is archived. You can implement it as-is and Kubo supports it, but it will not evolve; proposals for a successor API go through the <a href="https://specs.ipfs.tech/meta/spec-for-specs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IPIP process<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a>.</p> <p>Learn more about the <a href="https://github.com/ipfs/pinning-services-api-spec" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pinning Service API Spec<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a>.</p> <div class="custom-block callout"><p><strong>Make your pinning service available to the community</strong></p> <p>If you'd like to make your custom pinning service available to all IPFS users, we welcome your submissions.</p> <p>First, make sure your service works correctly by running the <a href="https://github.com/ipfs-shipyard/pinning-service-compliance" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">pinning-service-compliance<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a> test suite (archived and unmaintained, but still usable for a one-off check).</p> <p>Once you're ready to open the doors to the public, create a pull request against the <a href="https://github.com/ipfs-shipyard/ipfs-webui" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IPFS Web UI GitHub repository<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a> in order to add it to the default list of pinning services that are displayed in the IPFS Desktop/Web UI Settings screen, and one of the core maintainers will be in touch.</p></div> <h2 id="other-options"><a href="#other-options" class="header-anchor">#</a> Other options</h2> <p>Pinning services that implement the vendor-agnostic <a href="https://ipfs.github.io/pinning-services-api-spec/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IPFS Pinning Service API<span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" x="0px" y="0px" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="15" height="15" class="icon outbound"><path fill="currentColor" d="M18.8,85.1h56l0,0c2.2,0,4-1.8,4-4v-32h-8v28h-48v-48h28v-8h-32l0,0c-2.2,0-4,1.8-4,4v56C14.8,83.3,16.6,85.1,18.8,85.1z"></path> <polygon fill="currentColor" points="45.7,48.7 51.3,54.3 77.2,28.5 77.2,37.2 85.2,37.2 85.2,14.9 62.8,14.9 62.8,22.9 71.5,22.9"></polygon></svg> <span class="sr-only">(opens new window)</span></span></a> specification are supported directly in IPFS Kubo itself. To learn more, run the <code>ipfs pin remote --help</code> command.</p></div> <div class="content-footer" data-v-5b0b93f5=""><div class="help-callout" data-v-bed3e0e4="" data-v-5b0b93f5=""><p data-v-bed3e0e4=""><b data-v-bed3e0e4="">Help us improve this site!</b></p> <p data-v-bed3e0e4=""><a href="https://github.com/ipfs/ipfs-docs/edit/main/docs/how-to/work-with-pinning-services.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-bed3e0e4="">Edit this page</a> <span data-v-bed3e0e4="">
